---
import CategoryLayout from '@/layouts/CategoryLayout.astro';
import { PROTECTOR_SPECS } from '@/data/specs';
import { categoryTitle } from '@/lib/seo';

const title = categoryTitle('Mattress Protectors', ['120–180 cm', 'Four-Corner Elastic']);
---

<CategoryLayout
  title={title}
  description="Hotel mattress protectors wholesale in 120, 150 and 180 × 200 cm with four-corner elastic. Polyester face and fill. MOQ 50 pcs."
  h1="Hotel mattress protectors"
  breadcrumb="Mattress Protectors"
  specs={PROTECTOR_SPECS}
  images={['hotel-mattress-protectors', 'hotel-mattress-protectors1']}
  specLead="Three sizes, four-corner elastic, polyester face and fill. Confirm whether the project needs a waterproof layer."
  supplierHref="/hotel-mattress-supplier/"
  supplierLabel="Hotel mattress supplier"
>
  <p>
    A protector does two jobs. It keeps spills and stains out of the mattress, and it adds a
    replaceable layer between the guest and a mattress that has to last a decade. The second job
    is the one housekeeping cares about, because a stained mattress cannot be cleaned back to
    white.
  </p>
  <p>
    Ours is polyester face and fill with elastic at the four corners, in 120, 150 and 180 × 200 cm.
    It sits over the mattress and under the fitted sheet.
  </p>

  <h2 class="pt-4 text-xl font-semibold text-ink-900">Fit, not size</h2>
  <p>
    The size on the label is the mattress, not the fabric. A 30 cm deep mattress and a 20 cm one
    take the same protector size and a different skirt depth. If the project uses both depths,
    say so; otherwise the deeper beds will pull the corners off by the second wash.
  </p>

  <h2 class="pt-4 text-xl font-semibold text-ink-900">Waterproof or not</h2>
  <p>
    The standard build is not a waterproof barrier. If the property needs one, that is a
    different laminate and a different price, and it should be specified before the order rather
    than discovered after the first complaint.
  </p>

  <h2 class="pt-4 text-xl font-semibold text-ink-900">Fire standard for pads</h2>
  <p>
    In the US, mattress pads fall under a separate cigarette-ignition standard from the mattress
    itself. If your project's spec sheet requires qualifying documents for the protector, send
    that line to us at inquiry so we can tell you what we can supply. We would rather answer
    honestly than assume the mattress paperwork covers the pad.
  </p>

  <h2 class="pt-4 text-xl font-semibold text-ink-900">Ordering with mattresses</h2>
  <p>
    Most of our protector volume ships with a mattress order. It saves a second freight booking
    and it means the property is not storing bare mattresses while a second container arrives.
    If you are buying both, put them on one inquiry and we will quote them together. Mattress
    builds and their fire documentation are on the
    <a class="font-semibold underline" href="/hotel-mattress-supplier/">hotel mattress supplier</a>
    page.
  </p>
</CategoryLayout>
